    {
      "kind": "topic",
      "text": "## Read this before the notation",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000024"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0001-flat-02",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "Δ-Nets is a proposed graph-rewriting model. Instead of walking a syntax tree, you turn a program into a graph of tiny nodes and wires, then repeatedly replace small matching pieces of that graph. The aim is optimal parallel reduction: do not spend effort on work that will later be thrown away, and do each necessary reduction once even when an expression is used in several places.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000025"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0001-flat-02",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "topic",
      "text": "### The core idea",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000026"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0001-flat-02",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "Build the program as a net of very small agents. Let local pairs interact on their own. Put sharing in the graph itself, not in a side table of copies.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000027"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0001-flat-02",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "topic",
      "text": "### The important caveat",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000028"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0001-flat-02",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "“Optimal” and the confluence guarantees here are the paper’s claims, argued in the linked source. This guide teaches the design. The definitions and proofs stay with the paper.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000029"
      ],
      "defines": [],
