    {
      "kind": "topic",
      "text": "## The anatomy of a connection",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000041"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0001-flat-03",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "In interaction nets, we model λ-terms as wiring. The λ-node has a binding port (for the parameter) and a body port (for the expression). The logic depends on how variables are distributed.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000042"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0001-flat-03",
      "annotations": [
